    "WATCH WATCH submenu Watch Live Record Your Match",
    "VISIT VISIT submenu Hotel Booking Sustainability Health & Wellness Shop",
    "Home >",
    "News >",
    "Three Americans Reach Quarterfinals at Orlando Open",
    "Thursday’s action at the Orlando Open saw the top two remaining seeds advance, while more upsets saw a pair of Americans knock off higher-seeded fellow countrymen en route to the quarterfinals.",
    "No. 1 seed Darian King of Barbados continued to cruise through the field with a second consecutive straight-sets win. Fifth-seeded Norbert Gombos of Slovakia, on the other hand, needed more than three hours and a third-set tiebreak to defeat American wild card Evan Song. King and Gombos will face off in the quarterfinals.",
    "Also advancing on Thursday were Americans Ulises Blanch, Marcos Giron, and wild card Michael Redlicki. Giron defeated No. 9 seed Dennis Novikov in straight sets, while Redlicki knocked off No. 11 seed Kevin King in a pair of all-American third round matches.",
    "Rounding out the singles quarterfinalists are No. 12 seed Gastao Elias of Portugal and No. 13 seed Nino Serdarusic of Croatia.",
    "The Orlando Open, which is a USTA Pro Circuit ATP Challenger event, is the first USTA Pro Circuit ATP Challenger event of the 2019 season and is the highest level of tennis on display to date at the USTA National Campus, with a prize-money pool of more than $54,000.",
    "Play continues Friday with the singles quarterfinals and doubles semifinals. Play begins at 11 a.m. Admission to the Orlando Open is free.",
    "For more information, including draws and full results, click here. All matches are being streamed live here.",
    "Thursday, January 3 – Results",
    "Singles Main Draw – Third Round",
    "(1) Darian King (BAR) def. (16) Johan Tatlot (FRA) 6-3, 6-3",
    "(5) Norbert Gombos (SVK) def. (WC) Evan Song (USA) 6-7(3), 7-5, 7-6(4)",
    "(12) Gastao Elias (POR) def. (7) Roberto Cid Subervi (DOM) 6-0, 6-4",
    "Marcos Giron (USA) def. (9) Dennis Novikov (USA) 6-1, 6-2",
    "(WC) Michael Redlicki (USA) def. (11) Kevin King (USA) 2-6, 6-2, 6-2",
    "(13) Nino Serdarusic (CRO) def. Stefan Kozlov (USA) 6-2, 7-5",
    "(14) Mathias Bourgue (FRA) def. (WC) Sam Riffice (USA) 6-4, 5-7, 6-2",
    "Ulises Blanch (USA) def. (LL) Gijs Brouwer (NED) 2-6, 6-3, 6-3",
    "Doubles Main Draw – Quarterfinals",
    "(1) Romain Areneodo (MON) / Andrei Vasilevski (BLR) def. Gonzalo Escobar (ECU) / Roberto Maytin (VEN) 7-5, 6-7(2), [10-6]",
    "(3) Goncalo Oliveira (POR) / Andrea Vavassori (ITA) def. Laurynas Grigelis (LTU) / Uladzimir Ignatik (BLR) 6-4, 6-2",
    "(4) Evan King (USA) / Hunter Reese (USA) def. Ulises Blanch (USA) / Sam Riffice (USA) 6-3, 6-4",
    "Luis David Martinez (VEN) / Andreas Siljestrom (SWE) def. JC Aragone (USA) / Alex Lawson (USA) 3-6, 7-6(6), [10-5]",
    "ABOUT THE USTA PRO CIRCUIT: With more than 100 tournaments throughout the country and prize money ranging from $15,000 to upwards of $160,000, the USTA Pro Circuit is the largest developmental tennis circuit in the world and the pathway to the US Open and tour-level competition for aspiring players. Now in its 40th year, the USTA Pro Circuit has been a launching pad for many of today’s top pros, including Andy Murray, Maria Sharapova, John Isner, Sloane Stephens, Kei Nishikori, Victoria Azarenka, Caroline Wozniacki and Garbine Muguruza. Follow the USTA Pro Circuit at #USTAProCircuit on social media and at www.procircuit.usta.com.",
